  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 711.02 Monitoring Location for Regulated Inorganics for Groundwater Systems",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 711.02 Monitoring Location for Regulated Inorganics for Groundwater Systems.\n\n(a) The sampling point for a PWS using groundwater (groundwater system) shall be at each entry point to the distribution system, as specified in the sampling schedule established pursuant to Env-Dw 708.01, so as to be representative of each well after treatment.\n\n(b) The O/O of a groundwater system shall collect each sample at the specified sampling point. If the O/O believes that conditions make another sampling point more representative of each source or treatment plant, the O/O shall request a change in sampling point pursuant to Env-Dw 708.04.\n\nSource. #9700, eff 5-1-10; ss by #12668, eff 1-1-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html"
